  "content": {
    "title": "Final Injury Report for Rockets-Warriors: Will Stephen Curry, Gui Santos Play?",
    "text": "The Golden State Warriors are at home on Sunday night as they host the Houston Rockets in a Western Conference matchup.Golden State enters Sunday’s game with a 36-41 record after losing at home to the Cleveland Cavaliers on Thursday night.Cary Edmondson-Imagn Images (Cary Edmondson-Imagn Images)In Thursday’s loss to the Cavaliers, Brandin Podziemski led the way for the Warriors as he recorded 25 points, four rebounds and four assists while Gui Santos added 25 points, four rebounds and four assists of his own.Now Golden State will try to bounce back on Sunday as they face off against the Rockets in a tough home matchup.On the other side, Houston enters Sunday’s contest with a 48-29 record after defeating the Utah Jazz at home in dominant fashion on Friday night.Houston Rockets forward Kevin Durant (7)Alonzo Adams-Imagn Images (Alonzo Adams-Imagn Images)Kevin Durant led the way for the Rockets in Friday’s victory as he ended the game with 25 points, five rebounds and six assists while Amen Thompson recorded 21 points, eight rebounds and four assists.While both teams are looking to pick up a victory in Sunday night’s matchup, both squads may be without multiple key players due to injuries.Rockets Injury ReportFor the Rockets, they have two players listed on their injury report as they have ruled out both Fred VanVleet and Steven Adams.Houston Rockets guard Fred VanVleet (5).© Darren Yamashita-Imagn Images (© Darren Yamashita-Imagn Images)Houston has ruled out VanVleet as he continues to recover from a torn ACL that he suffered during the offseason.Houston Rockets center Steven Adams (12) talks with head coach Ime UdokaChristopher Hanewinckel-Imagn Images (Christopher Hanewinckel-Imagn Images)The Rockets have also ruled out Adams as he is set to miss the remainder of the season while recovering from ankle surgery.Warriors Injury Report: Will Stephen Curry, Gui Santos Play?On the other side, the Warriors have seven players listed on their injury report, including both Stephen Curry and Santos.Golden State Warriors guard Stephen Curry (30)David Gonzales-Imagn Images (David Gonzales-Imagn Images)Golden State has listed Curry as questionable due to a lingering right knee injury that has sidelined him since Jan. 30 and he is expected to return on Sunday.The Warriors have also listed Seth Curry as questionable due to a thigh injury while Santos has been listed as probable and is expected to play despite dealing with right pelvic contusion.Golden State Warriors forward Gui Santos (15)Darren Yamashita-Imagn Images (Darren Yamashita-Imagn Images)Al Horford has been ruled out as he continues to recover from a calf injury while Quinten Post remains sidelined while recovering from a foot injury.Jimmy Butler and Moses Moody have also been ruled out as they are both set to miss the remainder of the season.Fans can catch Sunday night’s matchup between the Rockets and Warriors from the Chase Center at 10:00 p.m. ET on NBC and Peacock.This story was originally published by Athlon Sports on Apr 5, 2026, where it first appeared in the NBA section. Add Athlon Sports as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
